## Context

Child of tracker 0613 (goal 1), gap C. `Ticket-ref: tickets/0613`,
`Ticket-ref: tickets/0643`, `Ticket-ref: tickets/0033` — none close.

Ticket 0643's real, measured R22 run found the actual cause of gap C's
remaining `FAIL`: zoteus's `action:"stop"` durably cancels the currently
running job (checkpoint intact, nothing auto-resumes on its own) but does
not gate a subsequent EXPLICIT `action:"build"` call — call `build` again
right after `stop` and it happily resumes. `R22-pause-stops-background-work`'s
own wording ("after [stop] is used, a change that would create work creates
none") reads that as a fail, and the measurement backs it: `stop` → idle,
checkpoint intact (`passagesWithoutVectors:7`) → `build` again → resumes,
`work.embed.build.done` advances by 109 (`bench/results/
0643-resume-embedding-perturbation/acceptance-zoteus-r22-seeded.json`).

Author decision (2026-09-04): ask upstream, as a soft, non-demanding
proposal — same shape as issue #54 — rather than a bug report, since the
current behavior is reasonable for the common case and may be intentional.

## Action

Sent as [oscardvs/zoteus#56](https://github.com/oscardvs/zoteus/issues/56):
"Stopping a build doesn't keep it paused — `action:\"build\"` happily
resumes right after." Two shapes proposed, neither demanded: a persisted
`paused` flag `build`/`update` check and refuse against until cleared, or a
distinct `resume` action separate from `build`'s current resume/rebuild/repair
overload.

## What this does NOT do

Does not move `R22`'s graded verdict — it stays `FAIL`, correctly, until the
maintainer ships something and it is re-measured against a real build (see
0643's own "reverify after the fix merges" plan, author-directed). Does not
touch the staged, still-unsent `verification/UPSTREAM-PR-WORK-COUNTERS-0642.md`.

## Exit criteria

Issue sent, recorded in `SYNC.md` and `0613`'s log. Response tracking is
0613's business going forward, same as every other upstream item on this
tracker (#54, #55).
